===Glyph origin===
{{Han etym}}
{{liushu|i}} – An inverted {{l|zh|曰}} ("to speak"), hence [[亼]] with a horizontal stroke at the bottom, so the inverted mouth means "not to speak".

Another theory suggests that it depicts something in the mouth. Maybe the original form of {{och-l|噤}} or {{och-l|吟}}. The derivative {{och-l|含}} refers to the original word.

===Etymology 1===
{{zh-forms|alt=𫢉,⿱𠆢𬼽,𱎜}} <!-- Note: 𫝆 is Japanese alternative form, not Chinese. -->
Etymology not clear. The word's root may be {{och-l|其|id=2|this}} ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}).

